      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. Evaluate $\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}$ and round up.\n2. Evaluate $\\frac{9}{4}$ and round up.\n3. Evaluate $\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2$ and round up.\n\nTo solve the expression \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\), we will evaluate each part step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Evaluate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\)\nFirst, calculate \\(\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5\n\\]\nNext, round 1.5 up to the nearest integer:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil1.5\\right\\rceil = 2\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Evaluate \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\)\nCalculate \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n\\]\nNext, round 2.25 up to the nearest integer:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil2.25\\right\\rceil = 3\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Evaluate \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\)\nFirst, square \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\):\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right) = \\frac{81}{16} = 5.0625\n\\]\nNext, round 5.0625 up to the nearest integer:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil5.0625\\right\\rceil = 6\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum the results\nNow, add the results from each part:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 6 = 11\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
